  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "QR-TB-009",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "category": "correctness-conversation-reset-publication-authority",
      "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Components/Pages/ChatPage.razor.cs",
      "location": "163-185; src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/PreparedChatCoordinator.cs:223-225,778-786; src/dotnet/Vulgata.Web/Data/PreparedChatPublicationOwner.cs:156-173,379-380; tests/Vulgata.Tests/ChatPageTests.cs:128-173",
      "affected_requirement": "Plan Technical Context storage boundary and AD-7C; FR-029-FR-030; SC-006; T019-T020",
      "evidence": "The explicit 新对话 action increments a page-only version, cancels active tokens, and clears rendered turns, but it never resets the scoped coordinator's publication authority. The next same-mode/same-scope AskAsync therefore reads _publicationAuthority.CurrentCommit.Conversation and passes the prior validated questions, answers, handles, and Logical Document hints into retrieval as if it were a follow-up. The two new-conversation page tests assert only that old markup or a late answer is not rendered; neither asks the next question and inspects its Conversation State. The in-flight case is also not closed by cancellation alone: PublicationAuthority.Prepare and the terminal transition are independent of Reset, so a pre-reset candidate that wins the final cancellation sample can become current after the page has announced a new conversation. This contradicts the plan's explicit new-conversation discard boundary and makes hidden prior-conversation context influence a supposedly fresh request.",
      "correction_outcome": "Add public behavior REDs that accept a turn, invoke 新对话, then prove the next same-mode/same-scope retrieval receives an empty Conversation State; add the same proof when reset races an in-flight request and a progressive reveal. Route the page reset through one publication-authority-owned reset/generation boundary so every candidate is bound to the current conversation generation and no pre-reset candidate can activate or reactivate current state after reset. Preserve current re-fetch/revalidation and accepted-only reveal, then rerun convergence and quality review.",
      "earliest_owner": "implement"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "REVISE. QR-TB-005 is closed: cancellation observed after a published commit completes only the already accepted reveal and the focused cancellation vectors pass. QR-TB-006 is closed for the reviewed commit operation: the owner has one authoritative sample, no post-sample virtual elapsed-time call, a terminal state publication barrier, and no coordinator post-commit success assignment; its behavioral cancellation/deadline/scheduler/concurrent vectors pass. QR-TB-007 is closed: Unicode text-element schedule cost and the fixed 1,000 ms safety margin are prebound, equality/within-margin selects immediate reveal, and the page consumes the committed directive. QR-TB-008 is closed: the coordinator requires non-null typed recorder and publication-owner dependencies and production composition supplies the same scoped instances. The independent bounded Track B/B-INT matrix passed 428/428, Web/checkpoint evidence remains green, Story 12.4 is ancestral, and the correction delta adds no EF/model/migration, Story 12.4 contract, alternate retrieval/streaming path, Track C sink, or fake release evidence. However QR-TB-009 is a blocking conversation-isolation defect: the user-visible new-conversation action does not reset or generation-fence the owner-current committed Conversation State, so hidden prior context survives and can be reactivated across a reset. E2E, final Track B verification, and Track C must remain closed until a test-first correction, fresh convergence, and a new independent quality verdict."
}
